From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:33:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Dolby Vision: picture upscaling with FSR 1

The Vulkan engine can enlarge a picture with AMD FidelityFX Super
Resolution 1 (dvvk_set_scaler: EASU, or EASU then RCAS), as CroqueMr's
CB1 lets a viewer do, but Kodi had no way to ask for it.

Settings > Player > Dolby Vision gets Upscaling (1080p and above) and
Upscaling (below 1080p), CB1's two tiers (1920 wide or 1080 high and
above; smaller), each Bilinear (the default), FSR 1 or FSR 1 +
sharpening (DV_UPSCALER, DV_UPSCALER_SD). The adapter chooses the
method by each picture's source size and calls dvvk_set_scaler when it
changes; the engine applies it only to an enlarged picture. With both
at Bilinear Kodi never calls it, so the engine runs as before. A
library without the symbol stays bilinear and the settings are not
offered (they stay shown while one is saved); a method the library
refuses leaves the one it has, logged.

Player information shows Upscaling (Bilinear, FSR 1, FSR 1 +
sharpening) only while the engine enlarges the picture. The help text
gives FSR's cost (UHD 770, 1080p to 4K: about 13 and 14 ms a picture
against 5 for bilinear) and says it is not yet measured on slower GPUs.

Strings 45161 to 45166; Bilinear is 45105.
