+msgctxt "#45162"
+msgid "How YBLOD's engine enlarges a picture smaller than the screen, for videos of 1080p and above (a 1080p video on a 4K display, for example): Dolby Vision videos, and HDR videos it converts to SDR. Bilinear: the engine's usual scaling, the lightest on the GPU. FSR 1: AMD FidelityFX Super Resolution 1, with sharper edges. FSR 1 + sharpening: FSR 1 with its sharpening pass. FSR takes much more GPU time: on an Intel UHD 770 a 1080p picture enlarged to 4K takes about 13 ms with FSR 1 and 14 ms with sharpening, against 5 ms with Bilinear. On slower graphics (Intel N150, AMD Vega 8) it has not been measured yet, and 60 frames a second may no longer keep up: if the picture stutters or frames are dropped, go back to Bilinear. Pictures shown at their own size or made smaller are not affected. Applies to the next video."
